## Steps for .data file
#### 1. Create `(.pdb)` file for a single molecule  --> molstruct.pdb

```
HEADER    water
COMPND
SOURCE
HETATM    1  H   HOH     1       4.225   5.600  5.000
HETATM    2  H   HOH     1       5.775   5.600  5.000
HETATM    3  O   HOH     1       5.000   5.000  5.000
CONECT    1    3
CONECT    2    3
CONECT    3    1    2
END
```

#### 2. Write a `fill.inp` file and use in UBUNTU ```packmol < fill.inp```. This will give a (.pdb) file containing bunch of molecules.

```
tolerance 2.0
filetype pdb
output water_box.pdb
add_box_sides 1.0         ## adds CRYST1 record automatically

structure molstruct.pdb
  number 100
  inside cube 0. 0. 0. 20.
end structure

```


#### 3. Using `VMD`, open TK console and input these commands

```
package require topotools
topo guessatom element mass
topo guessbonds
topo guessangles
topo writelammpsdata F:\\sla_hiwi\\lammps_testRuns\\h2o_KCl\\packmol_files\\h2o.data full

```
